HST Office: a document tab with a running modal dialog is never parked; a new document opened meanwhile gets a window of its own.

On macOS a dialog is a child window of its parent. When another tab opened in the window (the "+"
menu, File > New, a file from Finder or a launcher, or a menu command that opens a new document),
the tab group parked (hid, orderOut) the tab that owned a running modal dialog and macOS hid the
dialog with it, while it still blocked the office: frozen application, only Force Quit (user report
on HST Office 1.0.2, HST > "Văn bản hành chính" from a Sheets tab; reproduced on a macOS runner,
probe run 44843837715).

- framework/inc/documenttabmodal.hxx (new): ownsModalDialog() reads vcl's modal count of a tab
  window (Window::IsInModalMode, raised by Dialog::ImplSetModalInputMode on the dialog parent's frame).
- DocumentTabGroup::chooseGroup: the window the user works in, or the module window used last, takes
  no new tab while a modal dialog runs on one of its tabs; the document opens in a new window.
- DocumentTabGroup::park: a tab with a running modal dialog stays shown (no focus change) and is
  parked by a 500 ms retry timer once the dialog has ended and it is still not the shown tab.

License: modified upstream files keep their license (MPL-2.0); new files MPL-2.0.
Test: CppunitTest_framework_hstdocumenttabmodal; macOS runner probe (scripts/macos/modal-probe.sh).
